# claude-kickoff .scanignore — paths the scanners skip (one glob per line, with a reason).
# Only ever add a path with a real reason; never to silence a genuine finding.

# selftest.sh embeds intentional FIXTURES (a fake private key block, an AWS
# example key id, a USING(true) policy) to prove the scanners catch them — these
# are test data, not real secrets/footguns.
scripts/selftest.sh

# auth-heal-selftest.sh drives the auth self-heal with intentional FAKE tokens
# (TESTTOK-* / sk-ant-oat01-FAKETESTTOKEN* / sk-ant-oat01-STILLBADTOKEN* — hermetic
# stubs, no real `claude`, no network; the suite even asserts the fake token round-trips)
# that the scanner's OAuth-prefix rule trips on. Test fixtures, not real secrets.
scripts/auth-heal-selftest.sh

# shim-env-seal-selftest.sh embeds an intentional FIXTURE AWS key (AKIA…) in a temp foreign
# repo to prove the scanner's fail-closed + GIT_DIR-seal behavior catches a real secret through
# a shim. Same class as selftest.sh above — test data, not a real secret; the whole point of the
# file is to exercise the secret gate. (Verified: only the AKIA fixture, no real credential.)
scripts/shim-env-seal-selftest.sh

# adopt-preview.html is a 3.5 MB BUNDLED artifact (one 324k-char minified line), not source.
# The generic "hardcoded credential literal" rule matches minified assignments like x="…"+n+"…"
# 36 times, and the complex-regex pass can hang on the long line. Verified 2026-07-22 to contain
# ZERO high-signal secrets (BEGIN PRIVATE KEY / AKIA / sk_live_ / ghp_ / sk-ant- / xoxb- / AIza
# all count 0). Excluded as a build artifact — NOT to silence a genuine finding.
mission-control/experiments/adopt-preview.html
# Same class, same verification (2026-07-22): a 3.4 MB bundle, one 302k-char line, ZERO
# high-signal secrets. Listed per-FILE, deliberately not `experiments/*` — that dir also holds
# real hand-written .mjs sources which must stay scanned.
